Hi,

I=E2=80=99m experiencing consistent kernel panics on my laptop when it=E2=
=80=99s running on
battery power and I plug it into the charger (during the transition from DC
to AC). At first, the system is running normally and the Wi-Fi icon still
shows =E2=80=9CConnected,=E2=80=9D but I immediately lose internet access, =
and 10 seconds
later a kernel panic occurs.

Hardware: MediaTek MT7902
Kernel version: 7.1.5-zen1-2-zen
OS: Arch Linux
Device: Asus Vivobook Go 14 E1404FA

Steps to reproduce:

   1. Boot the laptop in AC mode.
   2. Unplug the charger and switch to battery mode.
   3. Stay in battery mode for at least 2 minutes.
   4. Plug the charger back in.
   5. The device immediately loses its connection and goes into a kernel
   panic.

*Additional Context:*
The power-save setting was changed to "off" using the command sudo iw dev
wlan0 set power_save off

